        1. Search the web for the topic using multiple varied queries to get broad coverage.
        2. Fetch and read the most promising pages to gather detailed information.
        3. Save key findings as notes using the note-taking tool, categorizing them by topic
           (e.g., "definition", "history", "key finding", "statistic", "expert opinion").
           Always include the source URL when saving notes.
        4. After gathering enough information (at least 5-8 notes), retrieve all your notes
           and synthesize them into a comprehensive summary.

        Be thorough but efficient. Focus on factual, well-sourced information.
        When you have gathered sufficient information, present a well-structured final summary
        with sections and source citations.
        """,
};

// --- Get the research topic ---
Console.WriteLine("╔══════════════════════════════════════╗");
Console.WriteLine("║       AI Research Agent              ║");
Console.WriteLine("╚══════════════════════════════════════╝");
Console.WriteLine();

string topic;
if (args.Length > 0)
{
    topic = string.Join(' ', args);
}
else
{
    Console.Write("Enter a topic to research: ");
    topic = Console.ReadLine()?.Trim() ?? "";
}

if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(topic))
{
    Console.Error.WriteLine("No topic provided. Exiting.");
    return;
}

Console.WriteLine($"\nResearching: {topic}");
Console.WriteLine(new string('─', 50));

